md`# brain-feedback

Feedback about the Brain's page, written on the page. A note placed with \`@tomlarkworthy/annotate\` is filed as a \`feedback\` issue of \`brain-issues\`, and from then on the note shows that issue.

| | |
|---|---|
| Where | The Brain's own address, with the owner signed in. Not a portal, not a page opened with \`#verify=\`, not a file. \`feedbackOn\` says which. |
| Start one | The page menu, Annotate, Feedback; or select text and press the chip \`feedback\`. Click what the note is about, write, press **File**. |
| The default | A note that annotate makes with no kind is made a feedback note here (\`feedbackDefault\`): Note in the menu, the chip \`annotate\`, Annotate in the palette. The owner, 2026-10-11: "yes make it the default". A plain note has no File and nothing sends it; three of his were written as plain notes and taken as filed. A note of another kind (\`switchboard\`) is as before. So this page has no plain note. |
| What is filed | \`issue.open\` with kind \`feedback\`, the label \`annotation\`, the id \`fb-<note id>\`, the first line as the title, and \`about\` the Worker whose module was clicked (\`brain\` when it is none). The body is the text, one sentence that says where, and the anchor as JSON in a fence named \`annotation\`. |
| On page load | \`issue.list?label=annotation\`, then \`issue.get\` for each, and a note is placed for each at its anchor. Asked again every 30 s while the tab is visible; an issue is read again only when its \`updated_at\` moved. |
| What a note shows | Two things: the request as it was written, whole, and the latest state of the work with the id of the issue that state is of. Nothing of the comments, links or reviews (Tom, 2026-10-11: "the original request needs to be show. I think the jsut the latest state is good"). When the issue is done, the reason it was closed with as well. |
| Gathered | The loop closes a feedback issue when it has made it part of a project or linked it to another issue, which is before the work is done. Such a note reads the state of the first of those issues that is still open, with its id (\`building\` \`dashboards-…\`), follows those issues (\`feedbackFollows\`: its parent, and each issue it says a link of), and has no Remove. They are not in the list, so each is read with \`issue.get\` on every ask. One step: an issue they are part of in turn is not followed. |
| Closed | An issue closed with a reason and no parent or link reads its state and the reason for ${feedbackLimits.waitMs / 60000} minutes from the close, with the time Remove comes and no Remove: the loop closes an issue and links it afterwards, 15.5 s apart on the first note filed. The time is the page's clock against the event's. |
| Done | The note reads **Done**, and has **Remove**, when the issue is closed and so is every issue it follows; one that follows none, when those minutes have passed. The reason shown is the one each of those was closed with, after its id and state (\`proj done: …\`, \`proj rejected: …\`); the issue's own when it follows none. |
| Remove | On a done issue, Remove (or the note's own ×) takes the label \`annotation\` off with \`issue.label\`, so no page loads the note again. The issue stays in the record. On an open, gathered or just closed issue the × hides the note until the page is loaded again. A note not yet filed is deleted. |

No Worker and no table: the record is the issue. The label is the switch, so anyone who may label can take a note off every page; the loop's briefs say not to.

The cells of a note are kept in this module (\`home\` of the kind), not in the module the note points at. A note on a Worker's panel is then not part of that Worker's source when the page exports it.

A note's box can be moved; the new place is not kept. Text typed and not filed is lost on a reload.
`
// %%
// The Brain's own page, the owner signed in. A verify page runs a Worker's tests and is left alone.
feedbackOn = !!brainOrigin && !brainPortal && !!(brainWho && brainWho.owner) && !/[#&]verify=/.test(location.hash)
// %%
feedbackLimits = ({ title: 120, text: 4000, shown: 400, everyMs: 30000, waitMs: 300000, label: "annotation", kind: "feedback", home: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-feedback", fence: "`".repeat(3) + "annotation\n", says: "Annotated on the Brain's page: " })
// %%
// One sentence a reader of the issue can act on without the page.
// near: the text of the element under the note's tip, for a note that marks no text of its own.
feedbackWhere = (anchor = {}, near = "") =>
  feedbackLimits.says +
  [anchor.module && `module \`${anchor.module}\``, anchor.cell && `cell \`${anchor.cell}\``, anchor.quote && anchor.quote.exact ? `at the text "${String(anchor.quote.exact).slice(0, 200)}"` : near && `on the element that reads "${String(near).replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim().slice(0, 120)}"`].filter(Boolean).concat(anchor.module || anchor.cell ? [] : ["no cell"]).join(", ") + "."
// %%
feedbackBody = (text, where, near = "") => `${String(text).trim()}\n\n${feedbackWhere(where.anchor, near)}\n\n${feedbackLimits.fence}${JSON.stringify(where)}\n${"`".repeat(3)}`
// %%
// { text, anchor, box } of a body feedbackBody wrote, or null.
feedbackParse = (body) => {
  const s = String(body || ""), at = s.lastIndexOf(feedbackLimits.fence);
  if (at < 0) return null;
  const from = at + feedbackLimits.fence.length, end = s.indexOf("\n" + "`".repeat(3), from);
  try {
    const where = JSON.parse(s.slice(from, end < 0 ? undefined : end));
    if (!where || typeof where.anchor !== "object" || !where.anchor) return null;
    const head = s.slice(0, at), said = head.lastIndexOf("\n\n" + feedbackLimits.says);
    return { text: (said < 0 ? head : head.slice(0, said)).trim(), anchor: where.anchor, box: where.box || null };
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
// %%
// The issues a closed issue is waited for in: what it is part of, and what it says a link of. One step, not theirs in turn.
feedbackFollows = (issue) => (issue && issue.closed ? [...new Set([issue.parent, ...(issue.links || []).map((l) => l.to)].filter(Boolean))] : [])
// %%
// What a note shows of an issue's events: the last one that says something, and the reason it was closed with.
// followed: what issue.get answered for each of feedbackFollows(issue), in that order; undefined for one not read.
// done: closed, and so is each issue it is followed in. gathered: closed, and one of those is not, or was not read.
// A closed issue that follows none is done once it has been closed for waitMs, and settling until then: the loop
// closes an issue and then links it (15.5 s apart on fb-a2kw99i9wy), and Remove in between would be for good.
feedbackProgress = (ticket, followed = [], { now = Date.now(), waitMs = feedbackLimits.waitMs } = {}) => {
  const { issue, events = [] } = ticket;
  const who = (by = {}) => (String(by.holder || "").startsWith("secret:") ? by.holder.slice(7).replace(/^issues-/, "") : by.caller || "");
  const said = (e) => e.body || e.reason || (e.type === "linked" ? `${e.remove ? "no longer " : ""}${e.rel}${e.to ? " " + e.to : ""}` : e.type === "swapped" ? "moved to another workflow" : "");
  // Not the loop's cost record, a comment `cost {…}` after each round, which says nothing to the owner.
  const lastOf = (t) => [...(t.events || [])].reverse().find((e) => e.type !== "opened" && said(e) && !/^cost \{/.test(e.body || ""));
  const closingOf = (t) => [...(t.events || [])].reverse().find((e) => e.type === "moved" && e.to === t.issue.state);
  const reasonOf = (t) => ((e) => (e ? e.reason || "" : ""))(closingOf(t));
  const follows = feedbackFollows(issue), read = (id) => followed[follows.indexOf(id)];
  const stateOf = (id) => ((t) => (t ? `: ${t.issue.state}` : ""))(read(id));
  const until = ((e) => (e ? e.at : issue.updated_at || 0))(closingOf(ticket)) + waitMs;
  const done = !!issue.closed && (follows.length ? follows.every((id) => read(id) && read(id).issue.closed) : now >= until);
  const gathered = !!issue.closed && !done && follows.length > 0, settling = !!issue.closed && !done && !follows.length;
  const links = [issue.parent && `part of ${issue.parent}${stateOf(issue.parent)}`, ...(issue.links || []).map((l) => `${l.rel} ${l.to}${stateOf(l.to)}`)].filter(Boolean);
  // The later of the issue's own last event and those of the issues it is followed in, which is named.
  const last = [[null, lastOf(ticket)], ...follows.map((id) => [id, read(id) && lastOf(read(id))])].filter(([, e]) => e).sort((x, y) => y[1].at - x[1].at)[0];
  const reason = !issue.closed || gathered ? "" : follows.length ? follows.map((id) => `${id} ${read(id).issue.state}${reasonOf(read(id)) ? ": " + reasonOf(read(id)) : ""}`).join("\n") : reasonOf(ticket);
  // Where the work is now: the first issue it is followed in that is still open, else the issue itself.
  const open = follows.find((id) => read(id) && !read(id).issue.closed);
  const where = done ? { state: "Done", id: issue.id } : gathered ? (open ? { state: read(open).issue.state, id: open } : { state: "gathered", id: follows[0] }) : { state: issue.state, id: issue.id };
  return { state: issue.state, closed: !!issue.closed, done, gathered, settling, until, links, reason, where, last: last ? { who: who(last[1].by), at: last[1].at, type: last[1].type, text: (last[0] ? last[0] + ": " : "") + said(last[1]) } : null };
}
// %%
// The notes of one page. client: issue.* calls. store: annotate's (create, remove, patch, get, all, refresh).
feedbackApp = ({ client, store, about = () => "brain", near = () => "", limits = feedbackLimits, now = () => Date.now() }) => {
  // tickets: issue id to what issue.get answered. of: note id to issue id. hidden: open issues whose note was closed here.
  const tickets = new Map(), of = new Map(), els = new Map(), drafts = new Map(), says = new Map(), hidden = new Set(), filing = new Set();
  let busy = false;
  for (const a of store.all()) if (a.kind === limits.kind && a.issue) of.set(a.id, a.issue);
  const get = async (iss) => {
    const r = await client.query("issue.get", { id: iss });
    tickets.set(iss, r);
    return r;
  };
  const cut = (s, n) => (String(s).length > n ? String(s).slice(0, n) + "…" : String(s));
  const has = async (id) => (await store.refresh(), !!store.get(id));
  const progress = (t) => feedbackProgress(t, feedbackFollows(t.issue).map((f) => tickets.get(f)), { now: now(), waitMs: limits.waitMs });
  const view = (id) => {
    const iss = of.get(id), t = iss && tickets.get(iss), muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
    if (!iss) {
      const box = htl.html`<textarea rows="4" maxlength=${limits.text} placeholder="What is wrong or wanted here" style="font:inherit;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box">${drafts.get(id) || ""}</textarea>`;
      box.oninput = () => drafts.set(id, box.value);
      return htl.html`<div data-feedback="draft">${box}<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => file(id)}>File</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || "Filed as a feedback issue."}</span></div></div>`;
    }
    if (!t) return htl.html`<div data-feedback="filing" style=${muted}>${iss}…</div>`;
    const p = progress(t), w = feedbackParse(t.issue.body);
    return htl.html`<div data-feedback=${p.done ? "done" : p.gathered ? "gathered" : p.settling ? "closed" : "open"} style=${"border-left:3px solid " + (p.done ? "#2a9d4b" : "var(--theme-foreground-faint)") + ";padding-left:8px"}>
      <div><b>${p.where.state}</b> <code>${p.where.id}</code></div>
      <div data-feedback-asked style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(w ? w.text : t.issue.title, limits.text)}</div>
      ${(p.done || p.settling) && p.reason ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-reason style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(p.reason, limits.shown)}</div>` : ""}
      ${p.settling ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-wait style=${muted}>Remove is here from ${new Date(p.until).toLocaleTimeString()}, unless it has been made part of other work by then.</div>` : ""}
      ${p.done ? htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => remove(id)}>Remove</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || ""}</span></div>` : ""}
    </div>`;
  };
  const draw = (id) => els.get(id) && els.get(id).replaceChildren(view(id));
  const file = async (id) => {
    const text = String(drafts.get(id) || "").trim(), rec = store.get(id);
    if (!text || !rec) return (says.set(id, text ? "The note is gone." : "Write something first."), draw(id));
    const iss = "fb-" + id.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9-]/g, "").slice(0, 36);
    of.set(id, iss);
    filing.add(iss);
    draw(id);
    try {
      await client.procedure("issue.open", { key: "annotation/" + id, id: iss, title: cut(text.split("\n")[0], limits.title), body: feedbackBody(text, { anchor: rec.anchor, box: rec.box }, near(rec)), kind: "feedback", about: about(rec.anchor), labels: [limits.label] });
      await get(iss);
      drafts.delete(id);
      says.delete(id);
      store.patch(id, { issue: iss });
    } catch (e) {
      of.delete(id);
      says.set(id, "issue.open was refused: " + e.message);
    }
    filing.delete(iss);
    draw(id);
  };
  // Places a note for each labeled issue that has none here, and takes away a note whose issue lost the label.
  const sync = async () => {
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    try {
      const listed = (await client.query("issue.list", { label: limits.label, limit: 200 })).issues.filter((i) => !i.hidden);
      for (const i of listed) if (!tickets.has(i.id) || tickets.get(i.id).issue.updated_at !== i.updated_at) await get(i.id);
      // What a closed one is followed in is not listed here, so nothing says it moved: each is read on every ask.
      for (const f of new Set(listed.flatMap((i) => feedbackFollows(tickets.get(i.id).issue)))) await get(f).catch(() => tickets.delete(f));
      const placed = new Set(of.values()), ids = new Set(listed.map((i) => i.id));
      for (const i of listed) {
        const where = !placed.has(i.id) && !hidden.has(i.id) && feedbackParse(tickets.get(i.id).issue.body);
        if (!where) continue;
        const a = store.create(where.anchor, { kind: limits.kind, issue: i.id, ...(where.box ? { box: where.box } : {}) });
        if (a) of.set(a.id, i.id);
      }
      for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
        if (ids.has(iss) || filing.has(iss)) continue;
        const t = await get(iss).catch(() => null);
        if (t && (t.issue.labels || []).includes(limits.label)) continue;
        of.delete(id);
        tickets.delete(iss);
        els.delete(id);
        store.remove(id);
      }
      for (const id of els.keys()) draw(id);
    } finally {
      busy = false;
    }
  };
  // Run when the page's notes change. A filed note that is no longer a cell was removed by the reader: when its
  // issue is done (feedbackProgress) the label comes off, and no page loads it again.
  const gone = async () => {
    for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
      if (await has(id)) continue;
      of.delete(id);
      els.delete(id);
      const t = tickets.get(iss);
      if (!t) continue;
      if (!progress(t).done) hidden.add(iss);
      else {
        tickets.delete(iss);
        await client.procedure("issue.label", { key: `annotation/${iss}/removed`, id: iss, remove: [limits.label] }).catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: issue.label was refused: " + e.message));
      }
    }
    for (const id of [...drafts.keys()]) if (!of.has(id) && !(await has(id))) (drafts.delete(id), els.delete(id));
  };
  const remove = async (id) => {
    store.remove(id);
    await gone();
  };
  const note = (id) => {
    const el = htl.html`<div data-feedback-note=${id} style="font:13px var(--sans-serif)"></div>`;
    els.set(id, el);
    draw(id);
    return el;
  };
  // Annotate's menu, palette and selection chip each end in store.create, and the plain note is the first of each.
  // From this call until the function it answers is called, a note created with no kind is of this one.
  const byDefault = () => {
    const create = store.create;
    let on = true;
    const mine = (anchor, fields) => create.call(store, anchor, on && !(fields && (fields.kind || fields.src)) ? { ...fields, kind: limits.kind } : fields);
    mine.byDefault = limits.kind;
    store.create = mine;
    return () => ((on = false), void (store.create === mine && (store.create = create)));
  };
  const kind = { id: limits.kind, label: "Feedback", chip: "feedback", icon: "✉", order: 1, home: limits.home, box: { w: 280 }, note: ({ id }) => `feedbackNote(${JSON.stringify(id)})` };
  return { note, file, sync, gone, remove, byDefault, kind, tickets, of, hidden, drafts };
}
// %%
// The text under a note's tip: the first element there that is in a cell and not in annotate's own layer.
feedbackNear = (rec, { resolve = a2Anchors.resolve, doc = document } = {}) => {
  try {
    const at = resolve(rec.anchor), p = at && (at.kind === "rects" ? at.rects[0] && { x: at.rects[0].left + 2, y: at.rects[0].top + 2 } : at);
    const el = p && doc.elementsFromPoint(p.x, p.y).find((e) => e.closest(".observablehq") && !e.closest("[data-a2-layer],[data-a2-root]"));
    return el ? el.textContent || "" : "";
  } catch {
    return "";
  }
}
// %%
feedback = feedbackOn ? feedbackApp({ client: brainClient, store: a2Store, near: feedbackNear, about: (anchor) => ((m) => (m ? m.worker : "brain"))(((brainModules && brainModules.modules) || []).find((m) => m.module === (anchor || {}).module)) }) : null
// %%
// The cell a note is: annotate writes `feedbackNote("<id>")` into this module for the kind below.
feedbackNote = (id) => (feedback ? feedback.note(id) : htl.html`<i>Feedback notes are for the owner, signed in at the Brain's address.</i>`)
// %%
feedbackKind = {
  if (!feedback) return "off: " + (!brainOrigin ? "not a Brain's address" : brainPortal ? "a portal" : !(brainWho && brainWho.owner) ? "the owner is not signed in" : "a verify page");
  plugins.add("annotate-kinds", feedback.kind, { invalidation });
  return "registered the kind feedback";
}
// %%
// The owner, 2026-10-11, asked whether Feedback should be the kind of a note he makes on his page: "yes make it the default".
feedbackDefault = {
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  invalidation.then(feedback.byDefault());
  return "a note made with no kind is of the kind " + feedbackLimits.kind;
}
// %%
feedbackSync = {
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  // A note placed before annotate knows the kind would be written into the module it points at.
  feedbackKind;
  for (let i = 0; i < 400 && !a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 25));
  if (!a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind)) return "annotate has no kind " + feedbackLimits.kind;
  const tick = () => document.visibilityState === "visible" && feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  const timer = setInterval(tick, feedbackLimits.everyMs);
  invalidation.then(() => clearInterval(timer));
  await feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  return `asked at ${new Date().toISOString()}; ${feedback.of.size} notes`;
}
// %%
feedbackGone = {
  annotations;
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  await feedback.gone();
  return feedback.of.size;
}
// %%
// A tracker and annotate's store, in memory, for the tests.
feedbackRig = () => {
  const issues = new Map(), calls = [], cells = new Map();
  let n = 0, at = 1000, clock = null;
  const client = {
    query: async (method, q = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, q]);
      if (method === "issue.list") return { issues: [...issues.values()].filter((t) => t.issue.labels.includes(q.label)).map((t) => ({ ...t.issue, body: undefined })) };
      if (method === "issue.get") return issues.has(q.id) ? structuredClone(issues.get(q.id)) : Promise.reject(new Error("no such issue"));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    },
    procedure: async (method, b = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, b]);
      if (method === "issue.open") {
        if (client.refuse) throw new Error(client.refuse);
        return void issues.set(b.id, { issue: { id: b.id, title: b.title, body: b.body, kind: b.kind, about: b.about, labels: [...b.labels], state: "open", closed: false, links: [], parent: null, updated_at: ++at }, events: [{ type: "opened", at, by: { caller: "owner" } }], children: [] });
      }
      if (method === "issue.label") return void ((t) => ((t.issue.labels = t.issue.labels.filter((l) => !b.remove.includes(l))), (t.issue.updated_at = ++at)))(issues.get(b.id));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    }
  };
  // What the loop does to an issue between two reads.
  const say = (id, event, change = {}) => ((t) => (t.events.push({ at: ++at, by: { caller: "token", holder: "secret:issues-implementer-2" }, ...event }), Object.assign(t.issue, change, { updated_at: at })))(issues.get(id));
  const store = {
    all: () => [...cells.values()],
    get: (id) => cells.get(id) || null,
    create: (anchor, fields = {}) => ((a) => (cells.set(a.id, a), a))({ id: "a2t" + ++n, anchor, box: { dx: 120, dy: -80, w: 240 }, ...fields }),
    patch: (id, fields) => void (cells.has(id) && cells.set(id, { ...cells.get(id), ...fields })),
    remove: (id) => void cells.delete(id),
    refresh: async () => {}
  };
  // The page's clock: long after every event, until a test sets it.
  const now = () => (clock == null ? at + feedbackLimits.waitMs : clock);
  return { client, store, issues, calls, cells, say, at: () => at, setNow: (ms) => void (clock = ms), app: () => feedbackApp({ client, store, now, near: () => "  Services\n table ", about: (a) => (a.module === "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues" ? "brain-x-issues" : "brain") }) };
}
// %%
test_feedback_body_keeps_the_anchor_and_says_where = {
  const anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues", cell: "issuesView", pid: "_p1", surface: "text", quote: { prefix: "For ", exact: "your attention", suffix: "" } };
  const body = feedbackBody("  The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.  ", { anchor, box: { dx: 1, dy: 2, w: 280 } });
  expect(body.startsWith("The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.\n\nAnnotated on the Brain's page: module `@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues`, cell `issuesView`, at the text \"your attention\".\n\n")).toBe(true);
  expect(feedbackParse(body)).toEqual({ text: "The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.", anchor, box: { dx: 1, dy: 2, w: 280 } });
  // Text that has a fence of its own, and a body nobody wrote this way.
  const fence = "`".repeat(3);
  expect(feedbackParse(feedbackBody(`see ${fence}annotation\n{"anchor":1}\n${fence}`, { anchor: { cell: "x" } })).anchor).toEqual({ cell: "x" });
  expect([feedbackParse("plain"), feedbackParse(`${fence}annotation\nnot json\n${fence}`), feedbackParse(`${fence}annotation\n{"box":{}}\n${fence}`), feedbackParse(undefined)]).toEqual([null, null, null, null]);
  expect([feedbackWhere({}), feedbackWhere({ quote: { exact: "foo" } }), feedbackWhere({}, " Services\n table ")]).toEqual(["Annotated on the Brain's page: no cell.", "Annotated on the Brain's page: at the text \"foo\", no cell.", "Annotated on the Brain's page: on the element that reads \"Services table\", no cell."]);
  return "the text, the sentence and the anchor go into a body and come back; a body without an anchor is null";
}
// %%
test_feedback_file_opens_an_issue_and_the_note_shows_it = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), app = rig.app();
  const a = rig.store.create({ module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues", cell: "issuesView", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5 } }, { kind: "feedback" });
  const el = app.note(a.id), press = (name) => [...el.querySelectorAll("button")].find((b) => b.textContent === name).click();
  const until = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 100 && !f(); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10)); return !!f(); };
  expect(el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback).toBe("draft");
  // Nothing written: nothing is sent.
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.textContent.includes("Write something first."))).toBe(true);
  expect(rig.calls).toEqual([]);
  const type = (text) => ((box) => ((box.value = text), box.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true }))))(el.querySelector("textarea"));
  // A refusal is said in the note, the text is kept, and the note is still a draft.
  rig.client.refuse = "not now";
  type("The table is too wide\non a phone.");
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.textContent.includes("issue.open was refused: not now"))).toBe(true);
  expect([el.querySelector("textarea").value, app.of.size]).toEqual(["The table is too wide\non a phone.", 0]);
  rig.client.refuse = null;
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.querySelector("[data-feedback=open]"))).toBe(true);
  const sent = rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.open").at(-1)[1];
  expect(sent).toMatchObject({ key: "annotation/a2t1", id: "fb-a2t1", title: "The table is too wide", kind: "feedback", about: "brain-x-issues", labels: ["annotation"] });
  expect(feedbackParse(sent.body)).toEqual({ text: "The table is too wide\non a phone.", anchor: a.anchor, box: a.box });
  expect(sent.body.includes("Annotated on the Brain's page: module `@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues`, cell `issuesView`, on the element that reads \"Services table\".")).toBe(true);
  expect([el.textContent.includes("open"), el.textContent.includes("fb-a2t1"), el.textContent.includes("on a phone."), rig.store.get(a.id).issue, !!el.querySelector("textarea")]).toEqual([true, true, true, "fb-a2t1", false]);
  // A second app on the same page (the cell ran again) takes the filed note as its own and places no second one.
  const again = rig.app();
  await again.sync();
  expect([again.of.get(a.id), rig.cells.size]).toEqual(["fb-a2t1", 1]);
  return "an empty note sends nothing; a refusal keeps the text; File sends issue.open with the anchor and the note shows the issue";
}
// %%
// Three notes of the owner's, 2026-10-11 20:31 to 20:40 CEST, had no kind and no File (page-feedback-filed-twice-never-arrived).
test_feedback_a_note_made_with_no_kind_is_a_feedback_note = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), app = rig.app(), anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", cell: "healthView", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5 } };
  const plain = rig.store.create, until = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 100 && !f(); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10)); return !!f(); };
  // As annotate creates a plain note: no fields, and the record has no kind.
  expect(rig.store.create(anchor).kind).toBe(undefined);
  const back = app.byDefault();
  expect(rig.store.create.byDefault).toBe("feedback");
  const a = rig.store.create(anchor), el = app.note(a.id);
  expect([a.kind, el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, !!el.querySelector("textarea"), [...el.querySelectorAll("button")].map((b) => b.textContent)]).toEqual(["feedback", "draft", true, ["File"]]);
  // It files as a note of the kind does.
  ((box) => ((box.value = "The Health chart is not useful."), box.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true }))))(el.querySelector("textarea"));
  el.querySelector("button").click();
  expect(await until(() => el.querySelector("[data-feedback=open]"))).toBe(true);
  expect([rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.open").map((c) => [c[1].id, c[1].labels]), rig.store.get(a.id).issue]).toEqual([[["fb-" + a.id, ["annotation"]]], "fb-" + a.id]);
  // Empty fields and a box alone are no kind; another kind and a source of the caller's own are left as they are.
  expect([rig.store.create(anchor, {}).kind, rig.store.create(anchor, undefined).kind, rig.store.create(anchor, null).kind]).toEqual(["feedback", "feedback", "feedback"]);
  expect(rig.store.create(anchor, { box: { w: 300 } })).toMatchObject({ kind: "feedback", box: { w: 300 } });
  expect([rig.store.create(anchor, { kind: "switchboard" }).kind, rig.store.create(anchor, { src: "1 + 1" }).kind]).toEqual(["switchboard", undefined]);
  // The cell ran again: the app before puts its own back, the next one is over the store's own, and takes that away in turn.
  back();
  expect([rig.store.create === plain, rig.store.create(anchor).kind]).toEqual([true, undefined]);
  const one = app.byDefault(), two = rig.app().byDefault();
  one();
  expect(rig.store.create(anchor).kind).toBe("feedback");
  two();
  expect(rig.store.create(anchor).kind).toBe(undefined);
  return "a note created with no kind is a feedback note with File, and files; another kind is left; taken away, a plain note is plain";
}
// %%
test_feedback_load_places_a_note_for_each_labeled_issue = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-one", title: "One", body: feedbackBody("One", { anchor, box: { dx: 5, dy: 6, w: 300 } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "by-hand", title: "Labeled by hand", body: "no anchor", kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "other", title: "Not a note", body: feedbackBody("x", { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all()).toEqual([{ id: "a2t1", anchor, kind: "feedback", issue: "fb-one", box: { dx: 5, dy: 6, w: 300 } }]);
  // A second ask reads nothing again and places nothing again.
  const before = rig.calls.length;
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.calls.slice(before).map((c) => c[0]), rig.cells.size]).toEqual([["issue.list"], 1]);
  // Progress: a comment by the loop is read on the next ask, and drawn.
  const el = app.note("a2t1");
  rig.say("fb-one", { type: "commented", body: "Looking at the Services table now." });
  await app.sync();
  // A comment is read and is not drawn: the note is the request and the latest state.
  expect([rig.calls.slice(-1)[0], el.querySelector("[data-feedback-asked]").textContent, el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.textContent.includes("Looking at the Services table now.")]).toEqual([["issue.get", { id: "fb-one" }], "One", "open", false]);
  rig.say("fb-one", { type: "linked", rel: "cause", to: "services-table-width" }, { links: [{ rel: "cause", to: "services-table-width" }] });
  await app.sync();
  expect(el.textContent.includes("services-table-width")).toBe(false);
  // The label taken off elsewhere: the note leaves this page too, with no call of its own.
  rig.issues.get("fb-one").issue.labels = [];
  const calls = rig.calls.length;
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.cells.size, app.of.size, rig.calls.slice(calls).map((c) => c[0])]).toEqual([0, 0, ["issue.list", "issue.get"]]);
  return "one note for the issue with the label and an anchor; none for a body without one; progress is read when updated_at moves";
}
// %%
test_feedback_done_then_remove_takes_the_label_off = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  for (const id of ["fb-done", "fb-open"]) await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id, title: id, body: feedbackBody(id, { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  const idOf = (iss) => [...app.of].find(([, i]) => i === iss)[0], el = app.note(idOf("fb-done"));
  expect(el.querySelector("button")).toBe(null);
  rig.say("fb-done", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "The table scrolls sideways now: brain-x-page 1a2b3c." }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
  await app.sync();
  expect([el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.querySelector("[data-feedback-reason]").textContent]).toEqual(["done", "Done", "The table scrolls sideways now: brain-x-page 1a2b3c."]);
  // Remove: the cell goes, the label goes, and the next ask places nothing.
  el.querySelector("button").click();
  for (let i = 0; i < 100 && rig.issues.get("fb-done").issue.labels.length; i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10));
  expect(rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label")).toEqual([["issue.label", { key: "annotation/fb-done/removed", id: "fb-done", remove: ["annotation"] }]]);
  await app.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all().map((a) => a.issue)).toEqual(["fb-open"]);
  // The note of an open issue closed with annotate's own x: no call, hidden here, and back on the next load.
  rig.store.remove(idOf("fb-open"));
  await app.gone();
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length, rig.cells.size, [...app.hidden]]).toEqual([1, 0, ["fb-open"]]);
  const reloaded = rig.app();
  await reloaded.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all().map((a) => a.issue)).toEqual(["fb-open"]);
  return "a closed issue reads Done with its reason; Remove takes the label off once; an open one comes back on the next load";
}
// %%
// The loop closes a feedback issue when it is gathered into a project (fb-a2kw99i9wy, events 862 to 866 on cb4).
test_feedback_a_gathered_note_follows_what_it_is_part_of = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-dash", title: "Dashboards", body: feedbackBody("we should have a better abstraction for dashboards", { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "proj", title: "Dashboards share a series", body: "a spec", kind: "project", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  rig.say("proj", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "spec-review", reason: "The spec is written." }, { state: "spec-review" });
  rig.say("fb-dash", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "In the spec of a-name-that-was-refused." }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
  rig.say("fb-dash", { type: "linked", rel: "part-of", to: "proj" }, { parent: "proj" });
  rig.say("fb-dash", { type: "commented", body: "The project is proj." });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  const id = [...app.of.keys()][0], el = app.note(id), labels = () => rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length;
  const reads = (from) => rig.calls.slice(from).map((c) => c[0] + (c[1].id ? " " + c[1].id : ""));
  // Closed, and the project it is part of is not: not Done, no Remove, and the project's state is what it reads.
  expect([el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.querySelector("button"), el.querySelector("[data-feedback-reason]")]).toEqual(["gathered", "spec-review", null, null]);
  expect([el.querySelector("code").textContent, el.querySelector("[data-feedback-asked]").textContent, el.textContent.includes("The project is proj.")]).toEqual(["proj", "we should have a better abstraction for dashboards", false]);
  // The project is read again on each ask, though nothing listed moved; its last event is drawn when it is the later one.
  let from = rig.calls.length;
  await app.sync();
  expect(reads(from)).toEqual(["issue.list", "issue.get proj"]);
  rig.say("proj", { type: "moved", from: "spec-review", to: "building", reason: "The owner approved the spec." }, { state: "building" });
  await app.sync();
  expect([el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.querySelector("code").textContent, el.textContent.includes("The owner approved the spec."), el.querySelector("button")]).toEqual(["building", "proj", false, null]);
  // The box's x on it: hidden here, the label stays, and it is back on the next load.
  rig.store.remove(id);
  await app.gone();
  expect([labels(), [...app.hidden], rig.issues.get("fb-dash").issue.labels]).toEqual([0, ["fb-dash"], ["annotation"]]);
  const loaded = rig.app();
  await loaded.sync();
  const id2 = [...loaded.of.keys()][0], el2 = loaded.note(id2);
  expect([rig.store.all().map((a) => a.issue), el2.querySelector("b").textContent]).toEqual([["fb-dash"], "building"]);
  // The project is done: the note reads Done with the project's reason, and Remove takes the label off.
  rig.say("proj", { type: "moved", from: "building", to: "done", reason: "The dashboards share one series: brain-x-page 4d5e6f." }, { state: "done", closed: true });
  await loaded.sync();
  expect([el2.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, el2.querySelector("b").textContent, el2.querySelector("[data-feedback-reason]").textContent]).toEqual(["done", "Done", "proj done: The dashboards share one series: brain-x-page 4d5e6f."]);
  el2.querySelector("button").click();
  for (let i = 0; i < 100 && rig.issues.get("fb-dash").issue.labels.length; i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10));
  expect([labels(), rig.cells.size]).toEqual([1, 0]);
  // A link said of another issue is followed the same way; one that cannot be read is not done.
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-dup", title: "Dup", body: feedbackBody("Dup", { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "task", title: "A task", body: "", kind: "task", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  rig.say("fb-dup", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "The same report." }, { state: "closed", closed: true, links: [{ rel: "cause", to: "task" }, { rel: "related", to: "nowhere" }] });
  const open = (t) => feedbackProgress(rig.issues.get("fb-dup"), feedbackFollows(rig.issues.get("fb-dup").issue).map((f) => t[f]));
  expect(feedbackFollows(rig.issues.get("fb-dup").issue)).toEqual(["task", "nowhere"]);
  const shut = { issue: { id: "x", state: "done", closed: true }, events: [] };
  expect([open({}).done, open({ task: shut }).done, open({ task: shut, nowhere: { issue: { id: "nowhere", state: "open", closed: false, hidden: true }, events: [] } }).done, open({ task: shut, nowhere: shut }).done]).toEqual([false, false, false, true]);
  expect([feedbackFollows({ closed: false, parent: "proj" }), feedbackFollows(null)]).toEqual([[], []]);
  return "a closed note whose project is open reads gathered with the project's state and has no Remove; Done and Remove when the project is closed";
}
// %%
// The loop closed fb-a2kw99i9wy 15.5 s before it linked it (events 863, 865), and writes a cost comment after every round.
test_feedback_a_close_waits_for_its_link_and_a_cost_comment_is_not_progress = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  for (const id of ["fb-late", "fb-alone"]) await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id, title: id, body: feedbackBody(id, { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "proj", title: "A project", body: "", kind: "project", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  for (const id of ["fb-late", "fb-alone"]) rig.say(id, { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "In the spec of proj." }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
  const closedAt = rig.at(), app = rig.app();
  rig.setNow(closedAt + 15000);
  await app.sync();
  const idOf = (iss) => [...app.of].find(([, i]) => i === iss)[0], late = app.note(idOf("fb-late")), alone = app.note(idOf("fb-alone"));
  const reads = (el) => [el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.querySelector("button"), (el.querySelector("[data-feedback-reason]") || {}).textContent];
  // Closed a moment ago with a reason and nothing else: not Done yet, no Remove, and the x only hides it.
  expect([reads(late), reads(alone)]).toEqual([["closed", "closed", null, "In the spec of proj."], ["closed", "closed", null, "In the spec of proj."]]);
  expect(late.querySelector("[data-feedback-wait]").textContent.includes(new Date(closedAt + feedbackLimits.waitMs).toLocaleTimeString())).toBe(true);
  rig.store.remove(idOf("fb-alone"));
  await app.gone();
  expect([rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length, [...app.hidden]]).toEqual([0, ["fb-alone"]]);
  // The link arrives on a later ask: gathered, and it never read Done.
  rig.say("fb-late", { type: "linked", rel: "part-of", to: "proj" }, { parent: "proj" });
  rig.setNow(closedAt + 45000);
  await app.sync();
  expect([reads(late), late.querySelector("code").textContent]).toEqual([["gathered", "open", null, undefined], "proj"]);
  // Nothing was linked to the other within the wait: Done by its own reason, with Remove. One ms before, not.
  const of = (ms) => ((p) => [p.done, p.settling, p.gathered])(feedbackProgress(rig.issues.get("fb-alone"), [], { now: closedAt + ms }));
  expect([of(feedbackLimits.waitMs - 1), of(feedbackLimits.waitMs)]).toEqual([[false, true, false], [true, false, false]]);
  rig.setNow(closedAt + feedbackLimits.waitMs);
  const loaded = rig.app();
  await loaded.sync();
  const el = loaded.note([...loaded.of].find(([, i]) => i === "fb-alone")[0]);
  expect([reads(el).slice(0, 2), !!el.querySelector("button"), reads(el)[3], el.querySelector("[data-feedback-wait]")]).toEqual([["done", "Done"], true, "In the spec of proj.", null]);
  // The loop's cost record after a round is not what the note says of the project: the event before it is.
  rig.say("proj", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "awaiting-approval", reason: "pass (review round 2)." }, { state: "awaiting-approval" });
  rig.say("proj", { type: "commented", body: 'cost {"role":"reviewer","round":2,"tokens":106356}' });
  rig.say("fb-late", { type: "commented", body: 'cost {"role":"implementer","round":1}' });
  await app.sync();
  expect([late.textContent.includes("cost {"), feedbackProgress(app.tickets.get("fb-late"), [rig.issues.get("proj")]).last.text, late.querySelector("b").textContent]).toEqual([false, "proj: pass (review round 2).", "awaiting-approval"]);
  // An open issue that is part of another reads no state of it, and asks for nothing more.
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-open", title: "open", body: feedbackBody("open", { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  rig.say("fb-open", { type: "linked", rel: "part-of", to: "proj" }, { parent: "proj" });
  expect([feedbackFollows(rig.issues.get("fb-open").issue), feedbackProgress(rig.issues.get("fb-open")).links]).toEqual([[], ["part of proj"]]);
  return "a close with a reason alone is not Done for " + feedbackLimits.waitMs / 60000 + " min; a link made after it gives gathered; a cost comment is not shown";
}
// %%
// With annotate's own store, under a kind of the test's own: this page may have no kind feedback registered.
test_feedback_cells_stay_in_this_module_with_annotates_store = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), limits = { ...feedbackLimits, kind: "feedbacktest" }, app = feedbackApp({ client: rig.client, store: a2Store, limits });
  const until = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 200 && !(await f()); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 25)); return !!(await f()); };
  const off = plugins.add("annotate-kinds", { ...app.kind, note: () => "1 + 1" });
  const mine = () => a2Store.all().filter((a) => a.kind === limits.kind);
  try {
    expect(await until(() => a2Store.kindOf(limits.kind))).toBe(true);
    const anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5 } };
    await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-real", title: "Real", body: feedbackBody("Real", { anchor, box: { dx: 7, dy: 8, w: 300 } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
    await app.sync();
    expect(mine().map((a) => [a.issue, a.home, a.anchor.module, a.box])).toEqual([["fb-real", limits.home, "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", { dx: 7, dy: 8, w: 300 }]]);
    const id = mine()[0].id;
    // Moving the box writes the record again; it stays in this module, and the issue stays on it.
    a2Store.patch(id, { box: { dx: 9, dy: 9, w: 300 } });
    await a2Store.refresh();
    expect(mine().map((a) => [a.issue, a.home, a.box.dx])).toEqual([["fb-real", limits.home, 9]]);
    // A second app (the cell ran again) finds the note by what the record keeps.
    const again = feedbackApp({ client: rig.client, store: a2Store, limits });
    await again.sync();
    expect([again.of.get(id), mine().length]).toEqual(["fb-real", 1]);
    // Closed, then removed with the store's own remove (the box's x): the label comes off.
    rig.say("fb-real", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "done" }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
    await app.sync();
    a2Store.remove(id);
    await app.gone();
    expect([mine().length, rig.issues.get("fb-real").issue.labels, rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length]).toEqual([0, [], 1]);
    return "placed in " + limits.home + " for a note about another module; kept there after a move; removed with the label";
  } finally {
    for (const a of mine()) a2Store.remove(a.id);
    off();
  }
}
// %%
test_feedback_near_reads_under_the_anchor_and_a_kept_note_without_its_label_goes = {
  // The anchor is what is resolved, not the record, whose cell is the note itself.
  const asked = [], el = { closest: (s) => s === ".observablehq", textContent: "Services" }, layer = { closest: () => true, textContent: "the note" };
  const doc = { elementsFromPoint: (x, y) => (asked.push([x, y]), [layer, el]) };
  expect([feedbackNear({ cell: "annotation_x_note", anchor: { cell: "services" } }, { resolve: (a) => (asked.push(a), { kind: "point", x: 3, y: 4 }), doc }), asked]).toEqual(["Services", [{ cell: "services" }, [3, 4]]]);
  expect(feedbackNear({ anchor: {} }, { resolve: () => ({ kind: "rects", rects: [{ left: 10, top: 20 }] }), doc })).toBe("Services");
  expect(feedbackNear({ anchor: {} }, { resolve: () => { throw new Error("gone"); }, doc })).toBe("");
  // A note kept from before, whose issue lost the label while no page was open: read once, then taken away.
  const rig = feedbackRig();
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-old", title: "Old", body: feedbackBody("Old", { anchor: { cell: "x" } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  const a = rig.store.create({ cell: "x" }, { kind: "feedback", issue: "fb-old" });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.cells.size, app.of.size, rig.calls.slice(1).map((c) => c[0])]).toEqual([0, 0, ["issue.list", "issue.get"]]);
  return "near resolves the anchor; a kept note of an issue with no label is removed on the first ask";
}
// %%
test_feedback_is_off_away_from_the_owners_page = {
  expect(feedbackOn).toBe(!!brainOrigin && !brainPortal && !!(brainWho && brainWho.owner) && !/[#&]verify=/.test(location.hash));
  // The default kind of a note is set on the owner's page and nowhere else.
  expect([feedbackDefault === "off", a2Store.create.byDefault]).toEqual(feedbackOn ? [false, feedbackLimits.kind] : [true, undefined]);
  if (feedbackOn) return "on: this is the Brain's address with the owner signed in";
  expect([feedback, feedbackSync, feedbackNote("x").textContent]).toEqual([null, "off", "Feedback notes are for the owner, signed in at the Brain's address."]);
  expect(feedbackKind.startsWith("off: ")).toBe(true);
  return "off here (" + feedbackKind.slice(5) + "): no kind registered, no call made";
}
// %%
import {brainOrigin, brainPortal, brainWho, brainClient, brainModules} from "@tomlarkworthy/brain-shell"
// %%
import {a2Store, a2Anchors, annotations} from "@tomlarkworthy/annotate"
// %%
import {plugins} from "@tomlarkworthy/plugin-registry"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
